===Etymology 2===
[[Image:Small pitcher Iran Louvre MAO714.jpg|thumb|right|A '''pitcher''' for pouring liquids.]]
[[File:Nepenthes_rafflesiana_ant.jpg|thumb|Ant drinking from the '''pitcher''' (type of plant appendage) of a ''Nepenthes rafflesiana''.]]

From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|picher|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|pichier|lang=fro}}, {{term|pechier||small jug|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|goh|en}} {{term|pehhar|lang=goh}}, {{term|pehhāri||beaker, cup|lang=goh}} (compare {{etyl|ML.|-}} {{term|picarium|lang=la}}, alteration of {{term|bicarium|lang=la}}). More at {{l|en|beaker}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A wide-mouthed, deep [[vessel]] for holding [[liquid]]s, with a [[spout]] or protruding [[lip]] and a [[handle]]; a [[water jug]] or [[jar]] with a large [[ear]] or handle.
# {{context|botany|lang=en}} A [[tubular]] or [[cuplike]] [[appendage]] or expansion of the leaves of certain plants. See [[w:pitcher plant|pitcher plant]].

